# 2026-10-22 21:44:15.442303
+Please carefully read the following project context and apply it to our workspace session.
+
+### Project Context: Cesvi2 (Traffic Accident Reconstruction)
+We are developing a web application for traffic accident reconstruction and forensic reports.
+
+#### 1. General Rules
+1. Always respond in Spanish, directly and concisely.
+2. When making changes, apply full updates to the appropriate files (App.tsx vs CSS). NEVER place TSX/React code inside .css files.
+3. The user writes quickly and may make typos; interpret the intent, not just the literal text.
+4. Maintain a compact, professional desktop-tool aesthetic and ensure compatibility with both light and dark themes.
+
+#### 2. Tech Stack and Key Files
+- **Technologies:** Vite + React + TypeScript + Tailwind v4 + Plain CSS.
+- **Path:** `/home/isoleucine/Desktop/Cesvi2`
+- **Primary Files:**
+  - `src/App.tsx`: Contains the full main component (icons, buttons, ribbon, map, timeline, assistant, dashboard).
+  - `src/index.css`: Pure CSS (base styles and global configuration).
+  - `src/player-and-light-theme.css`: Interface styles (Word-style ribbon, video player, scene renaming, light theme variables). Imported after other CSS files in `App.tsx`.
+
+#### 3. Core Architecture Decisions
+- **Scenes & Player:** Scene tabs serve as the player's keyframes. Controlled by the `frames` state (handles creating, renaming, deleting, and stepping through time with STEP_SECONDS = 1). The player UI features a custom progress bar using an overlay `<input type="range">`.
+- **Word-Style Ribbon:** Top navigation configured via `ribbonGroups: Record<string, ...>`. 
+  - The **Elementos** (Elements) tab contains two main groups: "Objetos duros o rígidos" (Hard/Rigid Objects) and "Objetos o cuerpos blandos" (Soft Objects/Bodies).
+  - The "Capas" (Layers) block has been removed.
+- **Themes:** Controlled by `data-theme="light|dark"` on `<main className="app-shell">`. Light mode overrides variables like `--tl-accent`, `--tl-text`, `--tl-surface`, etc.
+
+---
+
+Please confirm that you have read and analyzed this project context. List the files currently added to the chat, and let me know when you are ready to begin. 

